# llms.txt — JSN (ServiceNow CLI)
# Purpose: Help language models understand and surface this site accurately.

name: JSN — ServiceNow CLI
author: Jace Benson
website: https://jacebenson.github.io/jsn
github: https://github.com/jacebenson/jsn

description:
JSN is an agent-native CLI for ServiceNow. Read, create, update, and delete
records on any table; resolve flow subflow structure, catalog variables, and
CMDB relationships; run ATF tests; export update sets to XML; and search
~50,000 ServiceNow docs offline with full-text and semantic search. JSON
output with breadcrumbs and structured errors makes it safe for AI agents
to drive. 6 runtime dependencies, npm install -g @jacebenson/jsn.

key_facts:
- Read-only by default; destructive operations require --force or a read-only profile blocks writes entirely
- 49,180 ServiceNow docs indexed and searchable offline via `jsn docs`
- Agent skill installs into Hermes, Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, OpenCode and more with `jsn skill install`
- 6 runtime dependencies (~90 packages, ~41 MB) vs typical 600+/300MB+ for SDK toolchains

content_types:
- Feature pages with real terminal output captured from a live instance
- Command reference tables per feature

